VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is the Difference Between `call`, `apply`, and `bind`

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
In JavaScript, `call`, `apply`, and `bind` are methods that allow you to control the context (`this` value) in which a function is executed. While their purposes are similar, they differ in how they handle arguments and when the function is invoked.

  ---', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "What is the Difference Between `call`, `apply`, and `bind`", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
