INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # Strict Equality (`===`)

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
- Two strings are strictly equal if they have exactly the same sequence of characters and length.
    - Two numbers are strictly equal if they have the same numeric value.
      - **Special cases:**
        - `NaN === NaN` is `false`
        - `+0 === -0` is `true`
    - Two booleans are strictly equal if both are `true` or both are `false`.
    - Two objects are strictly equal if they refer to the **same object** in memory.
    - `null` and `undefined` are **not** strictly equal.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "# Strict Equality (`===`)", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
