VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is a pure function

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
A **pure function** is a function whose output depends only on its input arguments and produces no side effects. This means that given the same inputs, a pure function will always return the same output, and it does not modify any external state or data.

    Let''s take an example to see the difference between pure and impure functions,', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "What is a pure function", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
