INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you delete a cookie

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You can delete a cookie by setting the expiry date as a passed date. You don''t need to specify a cookie value in this case.
    For example, you can delete a username cookie in the current page as below.

    ```javascript
    document.cookie =
      "username=; expires=Fri, 07 Jun 2019 00:00:00 UTC; path=/;";
    ```

    **Note:** You should define the cookie path option to ensure that you delete the right cookie. Some browsers doesn''t allow to delete a cookie unless you specify a path parameter.

    **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

