INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is a callback function

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
A callback function is a function passed into another function as an argument. This function is invoked inside the outer function to complete an action.
    Let''s take a simple example of how to use callback function

    ```javascript
    function callbackFunction(name) {
      console.log("Hello " + name);
    }

    function outerFunction(callback) {
      let name = prompt("Please enter your name.");
      callback(name);
    }

    outerFunction(callbackFunction);
    ```

    **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

