INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is same-origin policy

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The same-origin policy is a policy that prevents JavaScript from making requests across domain boundaries. An origin is defined as a combination of URI scheme, hostname, and port number. If you enable this policy then it prevents a malicious script on one page from obtaining access to sensitive data on another web page using Document Object Model(DOM).

    **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

