INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you validate an email in javascript

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You can validate an email in javascript using regular expressions. It is recommended to do validations on the server side instead of the client side. Because the javascript can be disabled on the client side.

      ```javascript
      function validateEmail(email) {
        var re =
          /^(([^<>()\[\]\\.,;:\s@"]+(\.[^<>()\[\]\\.,;:\s@"]+)*)|(".+"))@((\[[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\.[0-9]{1,3}\])|(([a-zA-Z\-0-9]+\.)+[a-zA-Z]{2,}))$/;
        return re.test(String(email).toLowerCase());
      }
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

      The above regular expression accepts unicode characters.

