INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you loop through or enumerate javascript object

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You can use the `for-in` loop to loop through javascript object. You can also make sure that the key you get is an actual property of an object, and doesn''t come from the prototype using `hasOwnProperty` method.

      ```javascript
      var object = {
        k1: "value1",
        k2: "value2",
        k3: "value3",
      };

      for (var key in object) {
        if (object.hasOwnProperty(key)) {
          console.log(key + " -> " + object[key]); // k1 -> value1 ...
        }
      }
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

