INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What are the recommendations to create new object

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
It is recommended to avoid creating new objects using `new Object()`. Instead you can initialize values based on it''s type to create the objects.

      1. Assign {} instead of new Object()
      2. Assign "" instead of new String()
      3. Assign 0 instead of new Number()
      4. Assign false instead of new Boolean()
      5. Assign [] instead of new Array()
      6. Assign /()/ instead of new RegExp()
      7. Assign function (){} instead of new Function()

      You can define them as an example,

      ```javascript
      var v1 = {};
      var v2 = "";
      var v3 = 0;
      var v4 = false;
      var v5 = [];
      var v6 = /()/;
      var v7 = function () {};
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

