INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is tree shaking

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Tree shaking is a form of dead code elimination. It means that unused modules will not be included in the bundle during the build process and for that it relies on the static structure of ES2015 module syntax,( i.e. import and export). Initially this has been popularized by the ES2015 module bundler `rollup`, these days practically all bundlers use this technique.

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

154.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "What is tree shaking", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
