INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you detect a mobile browser without regexp

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You can detect mobile browsers by simply running through a list of devices and checking if the useragent matches anything. This is an alternative solution for RegExp usage,

      ```javascript
      function detectmob() {
        if (
          navigator.userAgent.match(/Android/i) ||
          navigator.userAgent.match(/webOS/i) ||
          navigator.userAgent.match(/iPhone/i) ||
          navigator.userAgent.match(/iPad/i) ||
          navigator.userAgent.match(/iPod/i) ||
          navigator.userAgent.match(/BlackBerry/i) ||
          navigator.userAgent.match(/Windows Phone/i)
        ) {
          return true;
        } else {
          return false;
        }
      }
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

