INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you make asynchronous HTTP request

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Browsers provide an XMLHttpRequest object which can be used to make asynchronous HTTP requests from JavaScript by passing the 3rd parameter as true.

      ```javascript
      function httpGetAsync(theUrl, callback) {
        var xmlHttpReq = new XMLHttpRequest();
        xmlHttpReq.onreadystatechange = function () {
          if (xmlHttpReq.readyState == 4 && xmlHttpReq.status == 200)
            callback(xmlHttpReq.responseText);
        };
        xmlHttpReq.open("GET", theUrl, true); // true for asynchronous
        xmlHttpReq.send(null);
      }
      ```

      Today this is considered deprecated, because an async `fetch` call (in browsers later than 2016) is simpler and more robust.

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

