INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is a rest parameter

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Rest parameter is an improved way to handle function parameters which allows us to represent an indefinite number of arguments as an array. The syntax would be as below,

      ```javascript
      function f(a, b, ...theArgs) {
        // ...
      }
      ```

      For example, let''s take a sum example to calculate on dynamic number of parameters,

      ```javascript
      function sum(...args) {
        let total = 0;
        for (const i of args) {
          total += i;
        }
        return total;
      }

      console.log(sum(1, 2)); //3
      console.log(sum(1, 2, 3)); //6
      console.log(sum(1, 2, 3, 4)); //10
      console.log(sum(1, 2, 3, 4, 5)); //15
      ```

      **Note:** Rest parameter is added in ES2015 or ES6

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

