INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you create an object with a prototype

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The `Object.create()` method is used to create a new object with the specified prototype object and properties. i.e, It uses an existing object as the prototype of the newly created object. It returns a new object with the specified prototype object and properties.

      ```javascript
      const user = {
        name: "John",
        printInfo: function () {
          console.log(`My name is ${this.name}.`);
        },
      };

      const admin = Object.create(user);

      admin.name = "Nick"; // Remember that "name" is a property set on "admin" but not on "user" object

      admin.printInfo(); // My name is Nick
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

