INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: List down the collection of methods available on WeakMap

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Below are the list of methods available on `WeakMap`,

      1. `set(key, value)`: Sets the value for the key in the `WeakMap` object. Returns the `WeakMap` object.
      2. `delete(key)`: Removes any value associated to the key.
      3. `has(key)`: Returns a Boolean asserting whether a value has been associated to the key in the `WeakMap` object or not.
      4. `get(key)`: Returns the value associated to the key, or undefined if there is none.
         Let''s see the functionality of all the above methods in an example,

      ```javascript
      var weakMapObject = new WeakMap();
      var firstObject = {};
      var secondObject = {};
      // set(key, value)
      weakMapObject.set(firstObject, "John");
      weakMapObject.set(secondObject, 100);
      console.log(weakMapObject.has(firstObject)); //true
      console.log(weakMapObject.get(firstObject)); // John
      weakMapObject.delete(secondObject);
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

