INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you decode an URL

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The `decodeURI()` function is used to decode a Uniform Resource Identifier (URI) previously created by `encodeURI()`.

      ```javascript
      var uri = "https://mozilla.org/?x=шеллы";
      var encoded = encodeURI(uri);
      console.log(encoded); // https://mozilla.org/?x=%D1%88%D0%B5%D0%BB%D0%BB%D1%8B
      try {
        console.log(decodeURI(encoded)); // "https://mozilla.org/?x=шеллы"
      } catch (e) {
        // catches a malformed URI
        console.error(e);
      }
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

