INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is the comma operator

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The comma operator is used to evaluate each of its operands from left to right and returns the value of the last operand. This is totally different from comma usage within arrays, objects, and function arguments and parameters. For example, the usage for numeric expressions would be as below,

      ```javascript
      var x = 1;
      x = (x++, x);

      console.log(x); // 2
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

