INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is the advantage of the comma operator

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
It is normally used to include multiple expressions in a location that requires a single expression. One of the common usages of this comma operator is to supply multiple parameters in a `for` loop. For example, the below for loop uses multiple expressions in a single location using comma operator,

      ```javascript
      for (var a = 0, b =10; a <= 10; a++, b--)
      ```

      You can also use the comma operator in a return statement where it processes before returning.

      ```javascript
      function myFunction() {
        var a = 1;
        return (a += 10), a; // 11
      }
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

