INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is a constructor method

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The constructor method is a special method for creating and initializing an object created within a class. If you do not specify a constructor method, a default constructor is used. The example usage of constructor would be as below,

      ```javascript
      class Employee {
        constructor() {
          this.name = "John";
        }
      }

      var employeeObject = new Employee();

      console.log(employeeObject.name); // John
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

