INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you get the prototype of an object

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You can use the `Object.getPrototypeOf(obj)` method to return the prototype of the specified object. i.e. The value of the internal `prototype` property. If there are no inherited properties then `null` value is returned.

      ```javascript
      const newPrototype = {};
      const newObject = Object.create(newPrototype);

      console.log(Object.getPrototypeOf(newObject) === newPrototype); // true
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

