INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you set the prototype of one object to another

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You can use the `Object.setPrototypeOf()` method that sets the prototype (i.e., the internal `Prototype` property) of a specified object to another object or null. For example, if you want to set prototype of a square object to rectangle object would be as follows,

      ```javascript
      Object.setPrototypeOf(Square.prototype, Rectangle.prototype);
      Object.setPrototypeOf({}, null);
      ```

