INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you get property descriptors of an object

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You can use the `Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptors()` method which returns all own property descriptors of a given object. The example usage of this method is below,

      ```javascript
      const newObject = {
        a: 1,
        b: 2,
        c: 3,
      };
      const descriptorsObject = Object.getOwnPropertyDescriptors(newObject);
      console.log(descriptorsObject.a.writable); //true
      console.log(descriptorsObject.a.configurable); //true
      console.log(descriptorsObject.a.enumerable); //true
      console.log(descriptorsObject.a.value); // 1
      ```

