INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What are the attributes provided by a property descriptor

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
A property descriptor is a record which has the following attributes

      1. `value`: The value associated with the property
      2. `writable`: Determines whether the value associated with the property can be changed or not
      3. `configurable`: Returns true if the type of this property descriptor can be changed and if the property can be deleted from the corresponding object.
      4. `enumerable`: Determines whether the property appears during enumeration of the properties on the corresponding object or not.
      5. `set`: A function which serves as a setter for the property
      6. `get`: A function which serves as a getter for the property

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

