INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do I modify the url without reloading the page

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The `window.location.href` property will be helpful to modify the url but it reloads the page. HTML5 introduced the `history.pushState()` and `history.replaceState()` methods, which allow you to add and modify history entries, respectively. For example, you can use pushState as below,

      ```javascript
      window.history.pushState("page2", "Title", "/page2.html");
      ```

      This mechanism is used by routing libraries of frameworks like React and Angular in order to simulate the behaviour of a multi-page-website, even though they are only SPA (Single Page Applications).

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

