INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you compare scalar arrays

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You can use length and every method of arrays to compare two scalars (compared directly using `===`) arrays. The combination of these expressions can give the expected result,

      ```javascript
      const arrayFirst = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
      const arraySecond = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
      console.log(
        arrayFirst.length === arraySecond.length &&
          arrayFirst.every((value, index) => value === arraySecond[index])
      ); // true
      ```

      If you would like to compare arrays irrespective of order then you should sort them before,

      ```javascript
      const arrayFirst = [2, 3, 1, 4, 5];
      const arraySecond = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5];
      console.log(
        arrayFirst.length === arraySecond.length &&
          arrayFirst
            .sort()
            .every((value, index) => value === arraySecond[index])
      ); //true
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

