INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is the difference between java and javascript

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Both are totally unrelated programming languages and no relation between them. Java is statically typed, compiled, runs on its own VM. Whereas JavaScript is dynamically typed, interpreted, and runs in a browser and nodejs environments. Let''s see the major differences in a tabular format,
      | Feature | Java | JavaScript |
      |---- | ---- | -----
      | Typed | It''s a strongly typed language | It''s a dynamic typed language |
      | Paradigm | Object oriented programming | Prototype based programming |
      | Scoping | Block scoped | Function-scoped, block scoped since ES6 |
      | Concurrency | Thread based | event based |

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

292.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "What is the difference between java and javascript", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
