INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Why do we call javascript as dynamic language

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
JavaScript is a loosely typed or a dynamic language because variables in JavaScript are not directly associated with any particular value type, and any variable can be assigned/reassigned with values of all types.

      ```javascript
      let age = 50; // age is a number now
      age = "old"; // age is a string now
      age = true; // age is a boolean
      ```

