INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What are enhanced object literals

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Object literals make it easy to quickly create objects with properties inside the curly braces. For example, it provides shorter syntax for common object property definition as below.

      ```javascript
      //ES6
      var x = 10,
        y = 20;
      obj = { x, y };
      console.log(obj); // {x: 10, y:20}
      //ES5
      var x = 10,
        y = 20;
      obj = { x: x, y: y };
      console.log(obj); // {x: 10, y:20}
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

