INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Does javascript uses mixins

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
JavaScript does not have built-in support for mixins as a formal language feature. However, developers commonly implement mixins using various patterns to enable code reuse and composition.

      A mixin is a way to add reusable functionality from one or more objects into a class or another object, without using classical inheritance. It promotes object composition by combining behaviors or properties from different sources into a single destination.

353.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "Does javascript uses mixins", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Mixin Example using Object composition

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
```javascript
      // Define a mixin
      const canEat = {
        eat() {
          console.log("Eating...");
        }
      };

      const canWalk = {
        walk() {
          console.log("Walking...");
        }
      };

      const canRead = {
        read() {
          console.log("Reading...");
        }
      };

      // Create a class
      class Person {
        constructor(name) {
          this.name = name;
        }
      }

      // Apply mixins
      Object.assign(Person.prototype, canEat, canWalk, canRead);

      // Use it
      const person = new Person("Sudheer");
      person.eat();  // Output: Eating...
      person.walk(); // Output: Walking...
      person.read(); // Output: Reading...
      ```
354.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "Mixin Example using Object composition", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
