INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is a thunk function

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
A thunk is just a function which delays the evaluation of the value. It doesn’t take any arguments but gives the value whenever you invoke the thunk. i.e, It is used not to execute now but it will be sometime in the future. Let''s take a synchronous example,

      ```javascript
      const add = (x, y) => x + y;

      const thunk = () => add(2, 3);

      thunk(); // 5
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

