INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you create self string using special characters

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The self string can be formed with the combination of `[]()!+` characters. You need to remember the below conventions to achieve this pattern.

      1. Since Arrays are truthful values, negating the arrays will produce false: ![] === false
      2. As per JavaScript coercion rules, the addition of arrays together will toString them: [] + [] === ""
      3. Prepend an array with + operator will convert an array to false, the negation will make it true and finally converting the result will produce value ''1'': +(!(+[])) === 1

      By applying the above rules, we can derive below conditions

      ```javascript
      (![] + [] === "false" + !+[]) === 1;
      ```

      Now the character pattern would be created as below,

      ```javascript
            s               e               l               f
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^

       (![] + [])[3] + (![] + [])[4] + (![] + [])[2] + (![] + [])[0]
       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^
      (![] + [])[+!+[]+!+[]+!+[]] +
      (![] + [])[+!+[]+!+[]+!+[]+!+[]] +
      (![] + [])[+!+[]+!+[]] +
      (![] + [])[+[]]
      ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
      (![]+[])[+!+[]+!+[]+!+[]]+(![]+[])[+!+[]+!+[]+!+[]+!+[]]+(![]+[])[+!+[]+!+[]]+(![]+[])[+[]]
      ```

      **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

364.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "How do you create self string using special characters", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
