VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is Lexical Scope?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Lexical scope is the ability for a function scope to access variables from the parent scope.

     ```js
     <script>
             function x(){
               var a=10;
               function y(){
                   console.log(a); // will print a , because of lexical scope, it will first look ''a'' in
               //its local memory space and then in its parent functions memory space
               }
               y();
           }
           x();
     </script>
     ```

