INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # 13. What is the output of below code

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
```javascript
const arrowFunc = () => arguments.length;
console.log(arrowFunc(1, 2, 3));
```

- 1: ReferenceError: arguments is not defined
- 2: 3
- 3: undefined
- 4: null

<details><summary><b>Answer</b></summary>
<p>', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "# 13. What is the output of below code", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: ## Answer: 1

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Arrow functions do not have an `arguments, super, this, or new.target` bindings. So any reference to `arguments` variable tries to resolve to a binding in a lexically enclosing environment. In this case, the arguments variable is not defined outside of the arrow function. Hence, you will receive a reference error.

Where as the normal function provides the number of arguments passed to the function

```javascript
const func = function () {
  return arguments.length;
};
console.log(func(1, 2, 3));
```

But If you still want to use an arrow function then rest operator on arguments provides the expected arguments

```javascript
const arrowFunc = (...args) => args.length;
console.log(arrowFunc(1, 2, 3));
```

</p>
</details>

---

**[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "## Answer: 1", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
