INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # 57. What is the output of below code ?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
- 1: console.log(true && ''hi'');
- 2: console.log(true && ''hi'' && 1);
- 3: console.log(true && '''' && 0);

<details><summary><b>Answer</b></summary>

- 1: hi
- 2: 1
- 3: ''''

Reason : The operator returns the value of the first falsy operand encountered when evaluating from left to right, or the value of the last operand if they are all truthy.

**Note:** Below these values are consider as falsy value

- 1: 0
- 2: ''''
- 3: null
- 4: undefined
- 5: NAN

</p>
</details>

