INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # 77. What is the output of below code?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
```javascript
const promiseOne = new Promise((resolve, reject) => setTimeout(resolve, 4000));
const promiseTwo = new Promise((resolve, reject) => setTimeout(reject, 4000));

Promise.all([promiseOne, promiseTwo]).then((data) => console.log(data));
```

- 1: [{status: "fulfilled", value: undefined}, {status: "rejected", reason: undefined}]
- 2: [{status: "fulfilled", value: undefined}, Uncaught(in promise)]
- 3: Uncaught (in promise)
- 4: [Uncaught(in promise), Uncaught(in promise)]

<details><summary><b>Answer</b></summary>
<p>', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "# 77. What is the output of below code?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: ## Answer: 3

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The above promises settled at the same time but one of them resolved and other one rejected. When you use `.all` method on these promises, the result will be short circuted by throwing an error due to rejection in second promise. But If you use `.allSettled` method then result of both the promises will be returned irrespective of resolved or rejected promise status without throwing any error.

```javascript
Promise.allSettled([promiseOne, promiseTwo]).then((data) => console.log(data));
```

</p>
</details>

