INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # 83. What is the time taken to execute below timeout callback?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
```javascript
console.log("Start code");

setTimeout(function () {
  console.log("Callback code");
}, 5000);

console.log("After callback");

let startTime = new Date().getTime();
let endTime = startTime;

while (endTime <= startTime + 10000) {
  endTime = new Date().getTime();
}

console.log("End code");
```

- 1: > 10 sec
- 2: Immediately
- 3: < 10 sec
- 4: <= 5sec

<details><summary><b>Answer</b></summary>
<p>', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "# 83. What is the time taken to execute below timeout callback?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: ## Answer: 1

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: JavaScript Core & DOM | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Even though there is a timer of 5 seconds supplied to `setTimeout` callback, it won''t get executed until the main thread is free and finished executing the remaining part of the code. In this example, the remaining code(while loop) takes 10seconds to finish it''s execution. In the mean time, the callback will be stored in callback queue upon completion of its 5 seconds timer. After 10 seconds, the callback will be moved to callstack because the callstack is empty by poping out global execution context.

</p>
</details>

**[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript Core & DOM", "subtopic": "## Answer: 1", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/javascript-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
