INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How to conditionally apply class attributes?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
You shouldn''t use curly braces inside quotes because it is going to be evaluated as a string.

    ```jsx harmony
    <div className="btn-panel {this.props.visible ? ''show'' : ''hidden''}">
    ```

    Instead you need to move curly braces outside (don''t forget to include spaces between class names):

    ```jsx harmony
    <div className={''btn-panel '' + (this.props.visible ? ''show'' : ''hidden'')}>
    ```

    _Template strings_ will also work:

    ```jsx harmony
    <div className={`btn-panel ${this.props.visible ? ''show'' : ''hidden''}`}>
    ```

    **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

61.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "How to conditionally apply class attributes?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
