INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Is it possible to use async/await in plain React?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Yes, you can use `async/await` in plain React, as long as your JavaScript environment supports ES2017+. Nowadays most modern browsers and build tools support ES2017+ version. If you''re using **Create React App**, **Next.js**, **Remix**, or any modern React setup, `async/await` is supported out of the box through **Babel**.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "Is it possible to use async/await in plain React?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
