INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is flux?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
**Flux** is an **application architecture** (not a framework or library) designed by Facebook to manage **data flow** in React applications. It was created as an alternative to the traditional **MVC (Model-View-Controller)** pattern, and it emphasizes a **unidirectional data flow** to make state changes more predictable and easier to debug.

       Flux complements React by organizing the way data moves through your application, especially in large-scale or complex projects.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "What is flux?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
