INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is the difference between Flow and PropTypes?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Flow is a _static analysis tool_ (static checker) which uses a superset of the language, allowing you to add type annotations to all of your code and catch an entire class of bugs at compile time.

     PropTypes is a _basic type checker_ (runtime checker) which has been patched onto React. It can''t check anything other than the types of the props being passed to a given component. If you want more flexible typechecking for your entire project Flow/TypeScript are appropriate choices.

**[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

143.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "What is the difference between Flow and PropTypes?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
