INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: What is NextJS and major features of it?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Next.js is a popular and lightweight framework for static and server‑rendered applications built with React. It also provides styling and routing solutions. Below are the major features provided by NextJS,

     1. Server-rendered by default
     2. Automatic code splitting for faster page loads
     3. Simple client-side routing (page based)
     4. Webpack-based dev environment which supports (HMR)
     5. Able to implement with Express or any other Node.js HTTP server
     6. Customizable with your own Babel and Webpack configurations

