INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # **1. Virtual DOM & Component Rendering**

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
React doesn''t manipulate the real DOM directly. Instead, it uses a **Virtual DOM** — a lightweight JavaScript representation of the UI.

     When a component renders (e.g., `<App />`):

        *   React **executes the component function** (e.g., `App()`).
        *   Hooks like `useState` are registered and tracked in order.
        *   React builds a **Virtual DOM tree** from the returned JSX.
        *   This virtual DOM is a **plain JS object** that describes the desired UI.

     This process ensures fast and efficient rendering before React decides how to update the real DOM.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "# **1. Virtual DOM & Component Rendering**", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # 2. **React Fiber Architecture**

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
React’s core engine is called **Fiber**, introduced in React 16. Fiber is a reimplementation of the React reconciliation algorithm with the following capabilities:

        *   Breaks rendering work into **units of work** (fiber nodes).
        *   Enables **interruptible rendering** (important for responsiveness).
        *   Supports **priority scheduling** and **concurrent rendering**.

     Each Fiber node represents a component and stores:

        *   The component type (function/class).
        *   Props, state, and effects.
        *   Links to parent, child, and sibling fibers.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "# 2. **React Fiber Architecture**", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # 3. **Reconciliation (Diffing Algorithm)**

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
When state or props change:

        *   React re-executes the component to produce a new virtual DOM.
        *   It **compares the new virtual DOM to the previous one** using an efficient diffing algorithm.
        *   React determines the **minimal set of DOM changes** required.

     This process is known as **reconciliation**.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "# 3. **Reconciliation (Diffing Algorithm)**", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # 4. **Commit Phase (Real DOM Updates)**

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Once reconciliation is done:

        *   React enters the **commit phase**.
        *   It applies calculated changes to the **real DOM**.
        *   It also runs side effects like `useEffect` or `useLayoutEffect`.

     This is the only time React interacts directly with the browser DOM.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "# 4. **Commit Phase (Real DOM Updates)**", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
