VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # **Step 1 : Create the Context**

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Use `React.createContext()` to create a context object.
    
        ```jsx
        import React, { createContext } from ''react''; 
    
        const ThemeContext = createContext(); // default value optional
        ```
    
      You typically export this so other components can import it.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "# **Step 1 : Create the Context**", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
