VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Can you describe the useMemo() Hook?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The `useMemo()` Hook in React is used to **optimize performance** by **memoizing the result of expensive calculations**. It ensures that a function is **only re-executed when its dependencies change**, preventing unnecessary computations on every re-render.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "Can you describe the useMemo() Hook?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
