INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Can useRef be used to store previous values?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Yes, `useRef` is a common pattern when you want to compare current and previous props or state without causing re-renders.
        
        **Example: Storing previous state value**
        ```js
        import { useEffect, useRef, useState } from ''react'';
        
        function PreviousValueExample() {
          const [count, setCount] = useState(0);
          const prevCountRef = useRef();
        
          useEffect(() => {
            prevCountRef.current = count;
          }, [count]);
        
          const prevCount = prevCountRef.current;
        
          return (
            <div>
              <p>Current: {count}</p>
              <p>Previous: {prevCount}</p>
              <button onClick={() => setCount(c => c + 1)}>Increment</button>
            </div>
          );
        }
        ```
     
**[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

