The `useDeferredValue` hook is used to **defer updating a part of the UI** to keep other parts responsive. It accepts a value and returns a "deferred" version of that value that may lag behind. This is useful for optimizing performance when rendering expensive components.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "What is the useDeferredValue hook?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
