VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: How do you handle cleanup in useEffect?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
The cleanup function in `useEffect` is used to **clean up side effects** before the component unmounts or before the effect runs again. This prevents memory leaks, stale data, and unexpected behavior.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "React & Hooks", "subtopic": "How do you handle cleanup in useEffect?", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/sudheerj/reactjs-interview-questions/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
