INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # useFormState

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Manages form state and handles server responses:
     ```jsx
     ''use client''
     import { useFormState } from ''react-dom'';
     import { loginAction } from ''./actions'';

     export default function LoginForm() {
       const [state, formAction] = useFormState(loginAction, {
         errors: {},
         message: ''''
       });

       return (
         <form action={formAction}>
           <input name="email" type="email" />
           {state.errors.email && <p>{state.errors.email}</p>}
           
           <input name="password" type="password" />
           {state.errors.password && <p>{state.errors.password}</p>}
           
           <button type="submit">Login</button>
           {state.message && <p>{state.message}</p>}
         </form>
