INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # `renderToPipeableStream` example

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
```javascript
     import express from "express";
     import { renderToPipeableStream } from "react-dom/server";
     import App from "./App";

     const app = express();

     app.get("/", (req, res) => {
       const { pipe } = renderToPipeableStream(<App />, {
         onShellReady() {
           res.setHeader("Content-Type", "text/html");
           res.write("<!doctype html><html><body><div id=\"root\">");
           pipe(res);
         },
         onAllReady() {
           res.end("</div></body></html>");
         },
         onError(error) {
           console.error(error);
         },
       });
     });
     ```

     In practice, prefer `renderToPipeableStream` for React 18+ SSR because it improves perceived performance and works naturally with Suspense-driven progressive loading.

**[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

