INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Which is preferred option with in callback refs and findDOMNode()?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Topic**: React & Hooks | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
It is preferred to use _callback refs_ over `findDOMNode()` API. Because `findDOMNode()` prevents certain improvements in React in the future.

   The **legacy** approach of using `findDOMNode`:

   ```javascript
   class MyComponent extends Component {
     componentDidMount() {
       findDOMNode(this).scrollIntoView();
     }

     render() {
       return <div />;
     }
   }
   ```

   The recommended approach is:

   ```javascript
   class MyComponent extends Component {
     constructor(props) {
       super(props);
       this.node = createRef();
     }
     componentDidMount() {
       this.node.current.scrollIntoView();
     }

     render() {
       return <div ref={this.node} />;
     }
   }
   ```

   **[⬆ Back to Top](#table-of-contents)**

