VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Latency vs throughput

**Role**: Backend Developer | **Topic**: Server Architecture & Scaling | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
**Latency** is the time to perform some action or to produce some result.

**Throughput** is the number of such actions or results per unit of time.

Generally, you should aim for **maximal throughput** with **acceptable latency**.', '{"role": "Backend Developer", "role_id": "backend_developer", "topic": "Server Architecture & Scaling", "subtopic": "Latency vs throughput", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
