INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: ## Disadvantage(s): master-master replication

**Role**: Backend Developer | **Topic**: Server Architecture & Scaling | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
* You''ll need a load balancer or you''ll need to make changes to your application logic to determine where to write.
* Most master-master systems are either loosely consistent (violating ACID) or have increased write latency due to synchronization.
* Conflict resolution comes more into play as more write nodes are added and as latency increases.
* See [Disadvantage(s): replication](#disadvantages-replication) for points related to **both** master-slave and master-master.', '{"role": "Backend Developer", "role_id": "backend_developer", "topic": "Server Architecture & Scaling", "subtopic": "## Disadvantage(s): master-master replication", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: ## Disadvantage(s): replication

**Role**: Backend Developer | **Topic**: Server Architecture & Scaling | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
* There is a potential for loss of data if the master fails before any newly written data can be replicated to other nodes.
* Writes are replayed to the read replicas.  If there are a lot of writes, the read replicas can get bogged down with replaying writes and can''t do as many reads.
* The more read slaves, the more you have to replicate, which leads to greater replication lag.
* On some systems, writing to the master can spawn multiple threads to write in parallel, whereas read replicas only support writing sequentially with a single thread.
* Replication adds more hardware and additional complexity.', '{"role": "Backend Developer", "role_id": "backend_developer", "topic": "Server Architecture & Scaling", "subtopic": "## Disadvantage(s): replication", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
