INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: # Federation

**Role**: Backend Developer | **Topic**: Server Architecture & Scaling | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
<p align="center">
  
  <br/>
  <i><a href=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kKjm4ehYiMs>Source: Scaling up to your first 10 million users</a></i>
</p>

Federation (or functional partitioning) splits up databases by function.  For example, instead of a single, monolithic database, you could have three databases: **forums**, **users**, and **products**, resulting in less read and write traffic to each database and therefore less replication lag.  Smaller databases result in more data that can fit in memory, which in turn results in more cache hits due to improved cache locality.  With no single central master serializing writes you can write in parallel, increasing throughput.', '{"role": "Backend Developer", "role_id": "backend_developer", "topic": "Server Architecture & Scaling", "subtopic": "# Federation", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: ## Disadvantage(s): federation

**Role**: Backend Developer | **Topic**: Server Architecture & Scaling | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
* Federation is not effective if your schema requires huge functions or tables.
* You''ll need to update your application logic to determine which database to read and write.
* Joining data from two databases is more complex with a [server link](http://stackoverflow.com/questions/5145637/querying-data-by-joining-two-tables-in-two-database-on-different-servers).
* Federation adds more hardware and additional complexity.', '{"role": "Backend Developer", "role_id": "backend_developer", "topic": "Server Architecture & Scaling", "subtopic": "## Disadvantage(s): federation", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
