VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Database caching

**Role**: Backend Developer | **Topic**: Server Architecture & Scaling | **Difficulty**: Easy

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
Your database usually includes some level of caching in a default configuration, optimized for a generic use case.  Tweaking these settings for specific usage patterns can further boost performance.', '{"role": "Backend Developer", "role_id": "backend_developer", "topic": "Server Architecture & Scaling", "subtopic": "Database caching", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Easy", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
