INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Technical Interview Question: Security

**Role**: Backend Developer | **Topic**: Server Architecture & Scaling | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Technical Explanation & Model Answer
This section could use some updates.  Consider [contributing](#contributing)!

Security is a broad topic.  Unless you have considerable experience, a security background, or are applying for a position that requires knowledge of security, you probably won''t need to know more than the basics:

* Encrypt in transit and at rest.
* Sanitize all user inputs or any input parameters exposed to user to prevent [XSS](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cross-site_scripting) and [SQL injection](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SQL_injection).
* Use parameterized queries to prevent SQL injection.
* Use the principle of [least privilege](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Principle_of_least_privilege).', '{"role": "Backend Developer", "role_id": "backend_developer", "topic": "Server Architecture & Scaling", "subtopic": "Security", "category": "Theory", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/donnemartin/system-design-primer/master/README.md", "dataset_type": "Real-World-Curated-Online"}'::jsonb)
