INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write a C++ code to find the longest common substring in two strings.

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Write a C++ code to find the longest common substring in two strings.

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
#include <string>
#include <algorithm>

using namespace std;

string longestCommonSubstring(const string& s1, const string& s2) 
{ 
    int n1 = s1.length(); 
    int n2 = s2.length(); 
  
    int maxlen = 0;
    int endingIndex = n1;
            
    int dp[n1 + 1][n2 + 1]; 
  
    for (int i = 0; i <= n1; i++) { 
        for (int j = 0; j <= n2; j++) { 
            if (i == 0 || j == 0) { 
                dp[i][j] = 0; 
            } else if (s1[i - 1] == s2[j - 1]) { 
                dp[i][j] = dp[i - 1][j - 1] + 1; 
  
                if (dp[i][j] > maxlen) { 
                    maxlen = dp[i][j]; 
                    endingIndex = i; 
                } 
            } else { 
                dp[i][j] = 0; 
            } 
        } 
    } 
  
    return s1.substr(endingIndex - maxlen, maxlen); 
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript / DOM / React Tasks", "subtopic": "Write a C++ code to find the longest common substring in two strings.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
