INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Sort the given array using insertion sort

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Sort the given array using insertion sort
**Input Specification**:
```
[5, 1, 4, 2, 8]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def insertion_sort(arr):
    """
    Sort given array using insertion sort
    """
    # Traverse through the array 
    for i in range(1, len(arr)): 
        key = arr[i] 
  
        # Move elements of arr[0..i-1], that are 
        # greater than key, to one position ahead 
        # of their current position 
        j = i - 1
        while j >= 0 and key < arr[j] : 
            arr[j + 1] = arr[j] 
            j -= 1
        arr[j + 1] = key 
  
    return arr

arr = [5, 1, 4, 2, 8]
sorted_arr = insertion_sort(arr)
print(sorted_arr)
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Sort the given array using insertion sort", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
