INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Merge two sorted lists into a single sorted list

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Merge two sorted lists into a single sorted list
**Input Specification**:
```
list1 = [1,3,5,7] 
list2 = [2,4,6,8]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def merge_sorted_lists(list1, list2):
    merged_list = []
    i = 0
    j = 0

    # Iterate through the lists until all elements have been merged
    while (i < len(list1) and j < len(list2)):
        # If the element from the first list is smaller, add it 
        # to the merged list
        if list1[i] < list2[j]:
            merged_list.append(list1[i])
            i+=1
        # Otherwise add the element from the second list
        else:
            merged_list.append(list2[j])
            j+=1
 
    # Append any remaining elements from the first list
    while i < len(list1):
        merged_list.append(list1[i])
        i+=1
 
    # Append any remaining elements from the second list
    while j < len(list2):
        merged_list.append(list2[j])
        j+=1
 
    return merged_list
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Merge two sorted lists into a single sorted list", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
