INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Sort the following array using the merge sort algorithm.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Sort the following array using the merge sort algorithm.
**Input Specification**:
```
arr = [4, 10, 5, 1, 8, 9]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def merge_sort(arr):
    if len(arr) > 1: 
      mid = len(arr)//2
      left_arr = arr[:mid]
      right_arr = arr[mid:]

      merge_sort(left_arr)
      merge_sort(right_arr)

      i = j = k = 0

      while i < len(left_arr) and j < len(right_arr): 
        if left_arr[i] < right_arr[j]: 
            arr[k] = left_arr[i] 
            i+=1
        else: 
            arr[k] = right_arr[j] 
            j+=1
        k+=1
      while i < len(left_arr): 
        arr[k] = left_arr[i] 
        i+=1
        k+=1
      
      while j < len(right_arr): 
        arr[k] = right_arr[j] 
        j+=1
        k+=1
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Sort the following array using the merge sort algorithm.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Create an algorithm for searching for an element in a sorted array.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Create an algorithm for searching for an element in a sorted array.
**Input Specification**:
```
arr = [2, 4, 6, 8, 10]
target = 6
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def binary_search(arr, target):
  low = 0
  high = len(arr) - 1

  while low <= high: 
    mid = (low + high) // 2
    if arr[mid] == target: 
      return mid 
    elif arr[mid] < target: 
      low = mid + 1
    else: 
      high = mid - 1
  return -1
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Create an algorithm for searching for an element in a sorted array.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
