INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Create a program in C to find the difference between the smallest and the largest number in a given array.

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Create a program in C to find the difference between the smallest and the largest number in a given array.
**Input Specification**:
```
array = { 100, 2, 11, 1, 5, 34, 45 }
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
#include<stdio.h> 

// Function to find the difference between smallest and largest element in given array 
int findDifference(int array[], int n) 
{   
    int max = 0; 
    int min = array[0]; 
  
    // Find maximum and minimum element in array 
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)  
    { 
        if (array[i] > max) 
            max = array[i]; 
          
        if (array[i] < min) 
            min = array[i]; 
    } 
    return (max - min); 
} 

// Driver Code 
int main() 
{ 
    int array[] = { 100, 2, 11, 1, 5, 34, 45 }; 
    int n = sizeof(array)/sizeof(array[0]); 
    printf("Difference between largest and smallest element: %d",findDifference(array, n)); 
    return 0; 
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript / DOM / React Tasks", "subtopic": "Create a program in C to find the difference between the smallest and the larges", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
