VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write pseudocode to sort a given list of integers using bubble sort.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Write pseudocode to sort a given list of integers using bubble sort.

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
# Set a swap flag to true
swap = true 
# While the flag is true
while swap 
  # Set the swap flag to false
  swap = false
  # Iterate through the list
  for i in range(len(list) - 1):
    # Swap adjacent element if they are out of order
    if list[i] > list[i + 1]:
      temp = list[i]
      list[i] = list[i + 1]
      list[i + 1] = temp
      # Set the flag back to true
      swap = true
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Write pseudocode to sort a given list of integers using bubble sort.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
