VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write a code to generate a list of all possible permutations of a given string.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Write a code to generate a list of all possible permutations of a given string.
**Input Specification**:
```
"ABC"
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def get_permutations(string):
    if len(string) == 0:
        return []
    if len(string) == 1:
        return [string]
 
    permutations = []
    for i, char in enumerate(string):
        for permutation in get_permutations(string[:i] + string[i+1:]):
            permutations.append(char + permutation)
 
    return permutations

if __name__ == "__main__":
    print(get_permutations("ABC"))
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Write a code to generate a list of all possible permutations of a given string.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
