VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Create a Node.js server that can listen on port 8080.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Create a Node.js server that can listen on port 8080.

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
const http = require(''http'');

const hostname = ''127.0.0.1'';
const port = 8080;

const server = http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.statusCode = 200;
  res.setHeader(''Content-Type'', ''text/plain'');
  res.end(''Hello World\n'');
});

server.listen(port, hostname, () => {
  console.log(`Server running at http://${hostname}:${port}/`);
});
```

