INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Merge the following two sorted arrays into a single sorted array in Java.

**Role**: Java Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Merge the following two sorted arrays into a single sorted array in Java.
**Input Specification**:
```
[1, 5, 8]
[2, 3, 6]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
int[] mergeArrays(int[] array1, int[] array2) {
    int[] mergedArray = new int[array1.length + array2.length];
    int index1 = 0, index2 = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < mergedArray.length; i++) {
        if (index1 < array1.length 
            && (index2 >= array2.length || array1[index1] < array2[index2])) {
            mergedArray[i] = array1[index1];
            index1++;
        } else {
            mergedArray[i] = array2[index2];
            index2++;
        } 
    } 
    return mergedArray;
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Java Developer", "role_id": "java_developer", "topic": "Java DSA & OOP Problems", "subtopic": "Merge the following two sorted arrays into a single sorted array in Java.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
