INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Design an algorithm to sort an array using Quick Sort.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Design an algorithm to sort an array using Quick Sort.
**Input Specification**:
```
Array: [5, 3, 6, 2, 1, 4]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def quickSort(arr, low, high):
    # Base case
    if low >= high:
        return

    # Pivot is the middle element
    pivot = arr[(low + high) // 2]
    i = low # Left pointer
    j = high # Right pointer

    while i <= j:
        # If the current value is smaller or equal than the pivot
        while arr[i] < pivot:
            i += 1
        # If the current value is larger than the pivot
        while arr[j] > pivot:
            j -= 1

        # If values are not in the correct order
        if i <= j:
            arr[i], arr[j] = arr[j], arr[i]
            i += 1
            j -= 1

    # Recursively sort the left and right halves
    quickSort(arr, low, j)
    quickSort(arr, i, high)

arr = [5, 3, 6, 2, 1, 4]
quickSort(arr, 0, len(arr)-1)
print(arr)

Output: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Design an algorithm to sort an array using Quick Sort.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
