INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: What is the purpose of declaring an enum in Java?

**Role**: Java Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
What is the purpose of declaring an enum in Java?

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
The purpose of declaring an enum in Java is to clearly identify a set of related constants that can be tracked. Enums are used to define a special type that contains a fixed set of constants. Enums provide type safety and make the code more self-documenting. They also make it easier for the compiler to check for correct usage since enums can be easily identified.
```

