VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write an SQL query to select the most recent 5 orders for each customer.

**Role**: Database Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Write an SQL query to select the most recent 5 orders for each customer.
**Input Specification**:
```
customers: 

id  name  city
1    John  Paris
2    Adam   London
3   David  Paris
4    Mary  Tokyo

orders: 

id  customer_id   date
1      1           2020-02-20
2      1           2020-03-15
3      2           2020-02-09
4      2           2020-02-23
5      3           2020-01-14
6      3           2020-04-25
7      4           2019-11-15
8      4           2019-12-12
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
SELECT o.*
FROM orders o,
     (SELECT customer_id, MAX(date) as last_date 
      FROM orders
      GROUP BY customer_id) as last
WHERE o.customer_id = last.customer_id
AND o.date  >= (SELECT MAX(date) FROM orders WHERE customer_id = last.customer_id AND date < last.last_date)
ORDER BY o.customer_id, o.date DESC
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Database Developer", "role_id": "database_developer", "topic": "SQL Queries & Schema Design", "subtopic": "Write an SQL query to select the most recent 5 orders for each customer.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
