VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Develop a Java program to rotate a two-dimensional array clockwise by 90 degrees.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Develop a Java program to rotate a two-dimensional array clockwise by 90 degrees.
**Input Specification**:
```
[[1, 2], 
 [3, 4]]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
public class RotateMatrix 
{  
    public static void rotate(int[][] arr, int n) 
    {  
        for (int x = 0; x < n/2; x++) 
        {     
            for (int y = x; y < n-x-1; y++) 
            { 
                int temp = arr[x][y];  
                arr[x][y] = arr[y][n-1-x];  
                arr[y][n-1-x] = arr[n-1-x][n-1-y];  
                arr[n-1-x][n-1-y] = arr[n-1-y][x];  
                arr[n-1-y][x] = temp;  
            }  
        }  
    }  
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Develop a Java program to rotate a two-dimensional array clockwise by 90 degrees", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
