VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: How to check if a number is prime or not in Java

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
How to check if a number is prime or not in Java

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
public class Number { 
	
    public static boolean isPrime(int n) 
    { 
        // Corner cases 
        if (n <= 1) 
            return false; 
        if (n <= 3) 
            return true; 
  
        // This is checked so that we can skip 
        // middle five numbers in below loop 
        if (n % 2 == 0 || n % 3 == 0) 
            return false; 
  
        for (int i = 5; i * i <= n; i = i + 6) { 
            if (n % i == 0 || n % (i + 2) == 0) 
                return false; 
        } 
  
        return true; 
    } 
  
    public static void main(String[] args) 
    { 
        int n = 25; 
        if (isPrime(n)) 
            System.out.println("Yes"); 
        else
            System.out.println("No"); 
    } 
}
```

