INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Implement a function that will sort the array using insertion sort.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Implement a function that will sort the array using insertion sort.
**Input Specification**:
```
nums=[5,2,4,6,1,3]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def insertion_sort(nums):
    for i in range(1,len(nums)):
        item_to_insert = nums[i]
        j = i - 1
        while j >= 0 and nums[j] > item_to_insert:
            nums[j+1] = nums[j]
            j -= 1
        nums[j+1] = item_to_insert

    return nums


if __name__ == ''__main__'':
    nums = [5,2,4,6,1,3]
    print(insertion_sort(nums)) # Output: [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Implement a function that will sort the array using insertion sort.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
