INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Describe how to use a while loop in python.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Describe how to use a while loop in python.

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
A while loop in Python is a loop that runs until a certain condition is met. The syntax is similar to an if statement, but the condition is evaluated after each iteration of the loop. The code within the loop is executed until the condition evaluates to False.

Example:

i = 0
while i < 10:
    print(i)
    i += 1

This will print out the numbers from 0 to 9 as the condition is evaluated after each iteration.
```

