INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Create a C++ program to solve this problem

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Create a C++ program to solve this problem
**Input Specification**:
```
Given an array of integers, count the number of pairs of integers whose difference is K.

Example:
Input: array = [1, 7, 5, 9, 2, 12, 3], k = 2
Output: 4
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
#include <iostream>
#include <unordered_map>
using namespace std;

int countPairsWithDiffK(int arr[], int n, int k){
    // Create an empty unordered_map
    unordered_map<int, int> map;
     
    // Store count of all elements in map
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
        map[arr[i]]++; 
     
    int count = 0; 
 
    // Iterate through all elements and 
    // find number of elements with difference
    // equal to k.
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        if (map[arr[i] + k])
            count += map[arr[i] + k];
         
        if (map[arr[i] - k])
            count += map[arr[i] - k];
         
        // Decrease count for same numbers
        if (k == 0)
            count--;
    }
 
    return count / 2;
}
 
// Driver program
int main()
{
    int arr[] =  {1, 7, 5, 9, 2, 12, 3};
    int n = sizeof(arr) / sizeof(int);
    int k = 2;
     
    cout << countPairsWithDiffK(arr, n, k);
     
    return 0;
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript / DOM / React Tasks", "subtopic": "Create a C++ program to solve this problem", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
