#### Problem Description
Create a function to sort an array of objects by the property ''name'' in ascending order.
**Input Specification**:
```
const array = [
  {name: ''Bob'', age: 25},
  {name: ''Alice'', age: 19},
  {name: ''John'', age: 30},
  {name: ''Ben'', age: 27}
];
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
function sortByName(array) {
    array.sort(function(a, b) {
      var nameA = a.name.toUpperCase();
      var nameB = b.name.toUpperCase();
      if (nameA < nameB) {
        return -1;
      }
      if (nameA > nameB) {
        return 1;
      }
      return 0;
    });
    return array;
}
console.log(sortByName(array));
```

