VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Create a function to reversed an array in place.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Create a function to reversed an array in place.
**Input Specification**:
```
arr = [1, 2, 3, 4, 5]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def reverse_array(arr):
    start = 0
    end = len(arr) - 1
    while start < end:
        temp = arr[start]
        arr[start] = arr[end]
        arr[end] = temp
        start += 1
        end -= 1
    return arr

print(reverse_array(arr))
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Create a function to reversed an array in place.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
