**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Create a class in Python which has a method to sort an array of numbers in increasing order.
**Input Specification**:
```
nums = [4, 3, 1, 6]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
class ArraySort:
    def __init__(self, nums):
        self.nums = nums
    
    def sort(self):
        for i in range(len(self.nums)):
            for j in range(i+1, len(self.nums)):
                if self.nums[i] > self.nums[j]:
                    temp = self.nums[i]
                    self.nums[i] = self.nums[j]
                    self.nums[j] = temp
        return self.nums
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
