VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Explain what is Closure in Python Programming?

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Explain what is Closure in Python Programming?

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
In Python, a closure is a higher order function (a function that takes one or more functions as arguments or returns a function) that allows a function to remember or access the variables or arguments of the enclosing scope—even after the execution of the outer function has finished. A closure is created when a nested function is defined, and an inner function remembers the variables of its enclosing scope even after the execution of the outer function has finished.
```

