INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Design a data structure to find the first and last occurrence of a number in an array.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Design a data structure to find the first and last occurrence of a number in an array.
**Input Specification**:
```
array = [1, 5, 7, 8, 8, 10]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
class FindFirstLastOccurrence:
    def __init__(self, arr):
        self.arr = arr
        self.first_occurrence = -1
        self.last_occurrence = -1
    
    def findFirstLastOccurrence(self, k):
        #Find the first occurrence
        left = 0
        right = len(self.arr) - 1
        while left <= right:
            mid = (left + right) // 2
            if self.arr[mid] == k and (mid == 0 or self.arr[mid-1] < k):
                self.first_occurrence = mid
                break
            elif self.arr[mid] < k:
                left = mid+1
            else:
                right = mid-1
        #Find the last occurrence
        left = 0
        right = len(self.arr) - 1
        while left <= right:
            mid = (left + right) // 2
            if self.arr[mid] == k and (mid == len(self.arr)-1 or self.arr[mid+1] > k):
                self.last_occurrence = mid
                break
            elif self.arr[mid] > k:
                right = mid-1
            else:
                left = mid+1
        
        return self.first_occurrence, self.last_occurrence

if __name__ == "__main__":
    finder = FindFirstLastOccurrence([1, 5, 7, 8, 8, 10])
    print(finder.findFirstLastOccurrence(8)) # (3,4)
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Design a data structure to find the first and last occurrence of a number in an ", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
