INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write a Python program to find all the prime numbers in the range between 1 to 1000.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Write a Python program to find all the prime numbers in the range between 1 to 1000.

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
# Python program to find all the prime numbers in a 
# given range using Sieve of Eratosthenes 

def SieveOfEratosthenes(n): 
    # Create a boolean array "prime[0..n]" and 
    # initialize all entries it as true. A value   
    # in prime[i] will finally be False if i is 
    # Not a prime, else True. 
    prime = [True for i in range(n+1)] 
    p = 2
    while (p * p <= n): 
          
        # If prime[p] is not changed, then it is  
        # a prime 
        if (prime[p] == True): 
              
            # Update all multiples of p 
            for i in range(p * p, n+1, p): 
                prime[i] = False
        p += 1
    
    # Print all prime numbers 
    prime_nums_list = [] 
    for p in range(2, n): 
        if prime[p]: 
            prime_nums_list.append(p) 
    
    return prime_nums_list 
  
# Driver code 
n = 1000
print(SieveOfEratosthenes(n))
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Write a Python program to find all the prime numbers in the range between 1 to 1", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
