INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write a function in Python to merge two sorted arrays.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Write a function in Python to merge two sorted arrays.
**Input Specification**:
```
arr1 = [1, 5, 9]
arr2 = [2, 3, 6, 8]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def merge_sorted_arrays(arr1, arr2):
    n1, n2 = len(arr1), len(arr2)
    i, j, k = 0, 0, 0
    arr3 = [0] * (n1 + n2)

    while i < n1 and j < n2:
        if arr1[i] < arr2[j]:
            arr3[k] = arr1[i]
            i += 1
        else:
            arr3[k] = arr2[j]
            j += 1
        k += 1

    # Copy remaining elements 
    while i < n1:
        arr3[k] = arr1[i]
        i += 1
        k += 1

    while j < n2:
        arr3[k] = arr2[j]
        j += 1
        k += 1

    return arr3
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Write a function in Python to merge two sorted arrays.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
