```text
Type hinting is a feature of the Python language that allows one to add type information to a variable, a function, and its parameters. The type hinting allows Python to infer the type of data to be used and this helps the interpreter to identify any errors and provide more feedback during the development process. It also makes the code more readable and maintainable since type information can be used to provide auto-complete and better error messages.
