INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Compare inheritance and composition in Python

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Compare inheritance and composition in Python

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
Inheritance and composition in Python are two approaches for achieving code reuse. Inheritance involves creating a parent class which contains method and member field definitions. These are then used in a subclass and can be overridden to make them more specialized. Composition involves designing objects that contain references to other objects, using instance variables whose types are interfaces or classes. This way, the composition object can act as a proxy to the inner objects, passing requests on to them as required. The advantages of composition over inheritance include greater control over class dependencies and better encapsulation.
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Compare inheritance and composition in Python", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
