INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Design an algorithm to find the longest increasing subsequence in an array.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Design an algorithm to find the longest increasing subsequence in an array.
**Input Specification**:
```
input = [9, 8, 4, 12, 2, 10, 6, 14, 1, 16, 3, 11, 5, 15, 7]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def get_longest_increasing_subsequence(input):
    ''''''This algorithm will find the longest increasing subsequence in an array.''''''
    n = len(input)
    leng = [1]*n
    for i in range(n):
        for j in range(i):
            if(input[i] > input[j] and leng[i] < leng[j] + 1):
                leng[i] = leng[j]+1
    max_seq_len = max(leng)
    max_seq = []
    for i in range(n):
        if(leng[i] == max_seq_len):
            max_seq.append(input[i])
            max_seq_len -= 1
    max_seq.reverse()
    return max_seq

if __name__ == ''__main__'':
    input = [9, 8, 4, 12, 2, 10, 6, 14, 1, 16, 3, 11, 5, 15, 7]
    print(get_longest_increasing_subsequence(input))
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Design an algorithm to find the longest increasing subsequence in an array.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
