INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write a code to construct a BST with the elements 11, 18, 14, 6 and 7.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Write a code to construct a BST with the elements 11, 18, 14, 6 and 7.

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
# A node  
class Node:  
    def __init__(self,key): 
        self.left = None
        self.right = None
        self.val = key 

# A function to insert a new node with the given key  
def insert(root,node): 
    if root is None: 
        root = node 
    else: 
        if root.val < node.val: 
            if root.right is None: 
                root.right = node 
            else: 
                insert(root.right, node) 
        else: 
            if root.left is None: 
                root.left = node 
            else: 
                insert(root.left, node) 

# Create root node with the key 11  
root = Node(11)  
insert(root,Node(18))  
insert(root,Node(14))  
insert(root,Node(6))  
insert(root,Node(7))
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Write a code to construct a BST with the elements 11, 18, 14, 6 and 7.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
