VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Can you propose a C++ program for adding two matrices?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Can you propose a C++ program for adding two matrices?
**Input Specification**:
```
Matrix1 = [[2, 3],  
          [4, 5]]
 
Matrix2 = [[6, 7],  
          [8, 9]]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
#include <iostream> 
#define N 2 
  
// function to add two matrices 
void addMatrix(int A[][N], int B[][N], int C[][N]) 
{ 
    int i, j; 
    for (i = 0; i < N; i++) 
        for (j = 0; j < N; j++) 
            C[i][j] = A[i][j] + B[i][j]; 
} 
  
int main() 
{ 
    int A[N][N] = {{2, 3}, {4, 5}}; 
  
    int B[N][N] = {{6, 7}, {8, 9}}; 
  
    int C[N][N]; // To store result 
    addMatrix(A, B, C); 
  
    cout << "Resultant Matrix:\n"; 
    int i, j;
    // Print the resultant matrix 
    for (i = 0; i < N; i++) { 
        for (j = 0; j < N; j++) 
            cout << C[i][j] << " "; 
        cout << "\n"; 
    } 
    return 0; 
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
