INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Find the intersection of two sorted arrays in Java.

**Role**: Java Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Find the intersection of two sorted arrays in Java.
**Input Specification**:
```
arr1=[1, 2, 4, 5, 6]
arr2=[2, 3, 5, 7]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
public static int[] intersection(int[] arr1, int[] arr2) 
{ 
    // Initialise array to store intersection 
    int[] result = new int[arr1.length]; 
  
    // Initialise two index in both array 
    int i = 0, j = 0; 
  
    // Initially set intersection index 
    int k = 0; 
  
    // Sort both array 
    Arrays.sort(arr1); 
    Arrays.sort(arr2); 
  
    // Iterate over both array and store intersection 
    // in array result 
    while (i < arr1.length && j < arr2.length)  
    { 
        // If both current element are same 
        if (arr1[i] == arr2[j])  
        { 
            // Store it in result array 
            result[k++] = arr1[i++]; 
            j++; 
        } 
        // If first array current element is smaller 
        else if (arr1[i] < arr2[j]) 
            i++; 
        // If second array current element is smaller 
        else
            j++; 
    } 
  
    // return the result array 
    return Arrays.copyOfRange(result, 0, k); 
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Java Developer", "role_id": "java_developer", "topic": "Java DSA & OOP Problems", "subtopic": "Find the intersection of two sorted arrays in Java.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
