INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Explain the main difference between an array and a linked list.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Explain the main difference between an array and a linked list.

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
The main difference between an array and a linked list is that an array stores data items contiguously in memory, while a linked list stores them in individual elements linked together with references. An array can be accessed faster than a linked list since elements can be accessed directly by their index. On another hand, inserting and deleting elements from a linked list is faster since elements don''t have to be rearranged in memory like in an array. Additionally, linked lists can have an arbitrary number of elements unlike arrays which have a fixed size.
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Explain the main difference between an array and a linked list.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
