INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: List the advantages of using a linked list over an array.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
List the advantages of using a linked list over an array.

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
The advantages of using a linked list over an array include:

1. Insertion and deletion operations are faster since individual elements do not have to be rearranged in memory.
2. Elements can be stored in any order, as opposed to an array which requires elements to be stored contiguously.
3. Linked lists have an arbitrary number of elements, unlike an array which has a fixed size. 
4. Linked lists do not require the memory allocation of an entire block at once, making it suitable for dynamic memory allocation.
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "List the advantages of using a linked list over an array.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
