INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Implement the bubble sort algorithm for a linked list.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Implement the bubble sort algorithm for a linked list.
**Input Specification**:
```
link_list = [10->9->8->7->6]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
class Node:
    # initialization of node
    def __init__(self, data):
        self.data = data
        self.next = None
    
# bubble sort of linked_list
def bubble_sort(head):
    # Store last node
    end = None

    while end != head.next:
        p = head
        while p.next != end:
            q = p.next
            if p.data > q.data:
                p.data, q.data = q.data, p.data
            p = p.next
        end = p

# driver code
head =  Node(10) 
head.next = Node(9) 
head.next.next = Node(8) 
head.next.next.next = Node(7)
head.next.next.next.next = Node(6)
    
bubble_sort(head) 
<insert code to print the data of the linked list>
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Implement the bubble sort algorithm for a linked list.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
