INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write a code which takes two strings and prints its longest common subsequence.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Write a code which takes two strings and prints its longest common subsequence.
**Input Specification**:
```
String1: "ABCDGH"
String2: "AEDFHR"
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def longest_common_subsequence(str1, str2): 
    m = len(str1) 
    n = len(str2) 

    matrix = [[0 for x in range(n+1)] for x in range(m+1)] 

    for i in range(m+1): 
        for j in range(n+1): 
            if i == 0 or j == 0: 
                matrix[i][j] = 0
            elif str1[i-1] == str2[j-1]: 
                matrix[i][j] = matrix[i-1][j-1] + 1
            else: 
                matrix[i][j] = max(matrix[i-1][j], matrix[i][j-1]) 

    result = ""
    i = m 
    j = n 

    while i > 0 and j > 0: 

        if str1[i-1] == str2[j-1]: 
            result += str1[i-1] 
            i -= 1
            j -= 1

        elif matrix[i-1][j] > matrix[i][j-1]: 
            i -= 1
        else: 
            j -= 1
    
    return result[::-1] 

print(longest_common_subsequence("ABCDGH", "AEDFHR"))

Output:
ADH
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Write a code which takes two strings and prints its longest common subsequence.", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
