INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: What is the difference between a static method and an instance method in Python?

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
What is the difference between a static method and an instance method in Python?

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
A static method is a method that does not have access to the instance of the class and so it can''t be used to access instance variables. A static method is associated with the class itself, not with any particular instance. A static method is often used to create utility functions that don''t need to be accessed from instance level. 

An instance method requires an object or instance of a class to work. An instance method can access the instance variables of the class and has access to the self object which is an instance of the class. An instance method can also access static methods and static variables of the class.
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "What is the difference between a static method and an instance method in Python?", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
