#### Problem Description
What is a stack in Computer Science?

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
A stack is a data structure that works on the principle of Last in First Out (LIFO). It is used to store and retrieve elements in a particular order, and all operations of insertion and retrieval are performed at one end of the stack, referred to as the top. There are two main operations in a stack: Push - adds an item to the top, and Pop - removes an item from the top.
