VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: How would you differentiate a local variable from a global variable?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
How would you differentiate a local variable from a global variable?

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
A local variable is a variable declared within a block of code, usually within a function. When the block of code ends, the variable is no longer in scope and is destroyed. It is only accessible within the local scope. A global variable is declared outside of any function and is accessible by all code within the same scope. The scope of a global variable is the entire program or file.
```

