VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Create a function in Java that finds the difference between the largest and the smallest elements in a given array.

**Role**: Java Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Create a function in Java that finds the difference between the largest and the smallest elements in a given array.
**Input Specification**:
```
[1, 5, 10, 20]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
public static int arrayMaxMinDiff(int[] arr) {
	
	// Initialize greatest and smallest
  	int max = arr[0]; 
  	int min = arr[0]; 
  
 	// Iterate the array and find the max & min
  	for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    		if (arr[i] > max) 
      			max = arr[i]; 
    		if (arr[i] < min) 
      			min = arr[i]; 
  	}
  
  	// Calculate & return the difference
  	int diff = max - min; 
  	return diff; 
}
// Driver Code 
int[] arr = {1, 5, 10, 20}; 
int diff = arrayMaxMinDiff(arr); 
System.out.println("Difference between largest & smallest elements = " + diff); 
# Output
Difference between largest & smallest elements = 19
