INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Sort the elements of an array in ascending order using Bubble Sort algorithm in C++.

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Sort the elements of an array in ascending order using Bubble Sort algorithm in C++.
**Input Specification**:
```
arr[] = {4, 5, 2, 9, 3}
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;
  
int main() 
{ 
    int arr[] = {4, 5, 2, 9, 3};
    int n = sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0]); 
  
    // bubble sort algorithm 
    for (int i = 0; i < n-1; i++)      
     
        // Last i elements are already in place    
        for (int j = 0; j < n-i-1; j++)  
            if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) 
                swap(arr[j], arr[j+1]); 
  
    cout << "Sorted array: \n"; 
    for (int i=0; i < n; i++) 
        cout << arr[i] << " "; 
    cout << endl; 
  
    return 0; 
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript / DOM / React Tasks", "subtopic": "Sort the elements of an array in ascending order using Bubble Sort algorithm in ", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Medium", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING;
