VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Analyze and explain the output of the following C program.

**Role**: AI Engineer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Medium

#### Problem Description
Analyze and explain the output of the following C program.
**Input Specification**:
```
#include<stdio.h>
int main(){
 int x,y;
  x=2;
   y=++x*5;
   printf("%d\n",y);
}
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
The output of this program is "15". This is because the pre-increment operator (++) is used in the statement "y=++x*5". This means that the value of x is first incremented by 1 and then used in the statement. Therefore, the value of x is 3 and y is assigned the value 3*5 which is 15.
```

