INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Create a C program which implements the following algorithm:

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Create a C program which implements the following algorithm:
**Input Specification**:
```
Given an array of size n, print all distinct elements in the array in sorted order.
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
#include<stdio.h>

// A utility function to swap elements at two indexes in an array
void swap(int arr[], int i, int j)
{
	int temp = arr[i];
	arr[i] = arr[j];
	arr[j] = temp;
}

// Function to print distinct elements in an array
void printDistinct(int arr[], int n)
{
	// Pick all elements one by one
	for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)
	{
		// Check if the picked element is already printed
		int j;
		for (j=0; j<i; j++)
			if (arr[i] == arr[j])
				break;

		// If not printed earlier, then print it
		if (i == j)
			printf("%d ", arr[i]);
	}
}

// Driver program
int main()
{
	int arr[] = {6, 10, 5, 4, 9, 120, 4, 6, 10};
	int n = sizeof(arr)/sizeof(arr[0]);

	// Function calling
	printDistinct(arr, n);

	return 0;
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript / DOM / React Tasks", "subtopic": "Create a C program which implements the following algorithm:", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
