INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Write a code to multiply two matrices, assuming the two matrices can be multiplied.

**Role**: Python Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Write a code to multiply two matrices, assuming the two matrices can be multiplied.
**Input Specification**:
```
A = [[1, 2], [3, 4]] 
B = [[5, 6], [7, 8]]
```

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
def multiply_matrices(A, B):
    if len(A[0]) != len(B):
        raise ValueError("Matrices cannot be multiplied")

    rows_A = len(A)
    columns_A = len(A[0])
    rows_B = len(B)
    columns_B = len(B[0])

    result = [[0 for column in range(columns_B)] for row in range(rows_A)]

    for row in range(rows_A):
        for column in range(columns_B):
            for k in range(columns_A):
                result[row][column] += A[row][k] * B[k][column]

    return result
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Python Developer", "role_id": "python_developer", "topic": "Python Algorithms & Data Structures", "subtopic": "Write a code to multiply two matrices, assuming the two matrices can be multipli", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
