INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: What is the most efficient sorting algorithm for a large data set?

**Role**: Frontend Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
What is the most efficient sorting algorithm for a large data set?

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
The Quick Sort algorithm is one of the most efficient sorting algorithms for large data sets. It works by finding a pivot element in the array, and then dividing the array into two parts based on the pivot element. All elements that are lesser than the pivot element are placed to the left, and all elements that are greater than the pivot element are placed to the right. The Quick Sort algorithm then recursively divides and sorts the left and right parts until the entire array is sorted. It has a worst-case time complexity of O(n^2), but its average case time complexity is O(nlogn) which makes it an efficient sorting algorithm.
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Frontend Developer", "role_id": "frontend_developer", "topic": "JavaScript / DOM / React Tasks", "subtopic": "What is the most efficient sorting algorithm for a large data set?", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
