INSERT INTO public.document_embeddings (content, metadata)
VALUES ('### Real Coding Task: Create a JavaScript function to compare 2 strings to determine if they are anagrams (words with the same letters as each other).

**Role**: Java Developer | **Category**: Coding | **Difficulty**: Hard

#### Problem Description
Create a JavaScript function to compare 2 strings to determine if they are anagrams (words with the same letters as each other).

#### Verified Solution & Code Implementation
```text
function anagramCheck(str1, str2) {
  // Remove whitespace, convert strings to lowercase, and split into arrays
  let arr1 = str1.replace(/\s/g, '''').toLowerCase().split('''');
  let arr2 = str2.replace(/\s/g, '''').toLowerCase().split('''');
  
  // If the arrays are different lengths, they cannot be anagrams
  if (arr1.length !== arr2.length) {
    return false;
  }
  
  // Sort both arrays, and check if they are the same
  let sortedArr1 = arr1.sort();
  let sortedArr2 = arr2.sort();
  
  for (let i=0; i<sortedArr1.length; i++) {
    if (sortedArr1[i] !== sortedArr2[i]) {
      return false;
    }
  }
  return true;
}
```

#### Complexity & Quality Rubric
- **Validation**: Handles nominal and boundary test cases.
- **Best Practice**: Adheres to idiomatic design and standard time/space constraints.', '{"role": "Java Developer", "role_id": "java_developer", "topic": "Java DSA & OOP Problems", "subtopic": "Create a JavaScript function to compare 2 strings to determine if they are anagr", "category": "Coding", "difficulty": "Hard", "source": "https://github.com/sahil280114/codealpaca", "dataset_type": "Real-World-CodeAlpaca-20k"}'::jsonb)
